course: dictionary
lesson: 12233
title: Thinking about others
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A considerate person thinks about other people's feelings and needs, and acts kindly because of that. Considerate is a word for a good quality, like patience or sharing. «It was considerate of you to hold the door for Mr Patel.» Holding the door shows you thought about someone else before they had to ask.
explain: Considerate often goes with the word of: «considerate of others». You can be considerate in small ways, such as keeping your voice low when someone is trying to sleep or working quietly while your class is busy.
explain: Stories use considerate to show what a character is like. «Sam is considerate: he lets everyone have a turn on the swing.» The reader learns Sam is kind and careful of others, without being told so directly. Look for clues in what a character does, not only in what they say.
fact: Considerate means thinking about other people's feelings and needs, and acting kindly because of that.
fact: «Considerate» is an adjective. It can change to «more considerate» and «most considerate».
fact: A considerate action is thoughtful and helps others feel comfortable, such as holding a door or sharing.
fact: Phrases to remember: «considerate of others», «it was considerate of you to …», and «be considerate».
fact: The opposite of considerate is thoughtless, which means not thinking about how your actions affect other people.
exercise: «It was considerate of you to hold the door for me.» What does considerate mean here? | Loud and cheerful | Lost and confused | *Thinking about others and being kind to them | Quick and careless
exercise: Ravi keeps his voice low while the others are working. Which word describes him? | Lazy | Noisy | *Considerate | Greedy
exercise: «Sam is considerate: he lets everyone have a turn on the swing.» Find and copy the one word that means thinking kindly of others. | turn | swing | *considerate | everyone
test: A considerate person does what? | Ignores people who look sad | *Thinks about other people's feelings and needs | Shouts the loudest in class | Takes the last biscuit without asking
test: Which action is considerate? | Taking the biggest share of the cake | Talking loudly during a film | Pushing to the front of the queue | *Waiting your turn in the queue
exam: Which sentence shows a considerate friend? | Mia laughs loudly when Ben trips over | *Ali asks quietly if the others need help before he sits down | Ella notices Jo has no crayons and shares hers without being asked | Tom takes the ball and won't let anyone else play
